// Invariant 1: parser_validity
//   insideConstrainedOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut)
//
// Phase 1 preamble (loop with !insideConstrainedOut guard):
//   The loop guard keeps insideConstrainedOut false so the implication is
//   vacuously true on entry. The only path that sets insideConstrainedOut:=true
//   is RenderedEndsWith(generated, "<<") being satisfied, at which point we set
//   currentConstrainedOut := [] which satisfies IsValidPrefix([]) by method
//   precondition. EOS break leaves insideConstrainedOut false.
//
// Phase 2 (OpenConstrainedSpan):
//   Only runs when !insideConstrainedOut. Helper sets currentConstrainedOut := [];
//   IsValidPrefix([]) holds by method precondition. insideConstrainedOut := true.
//
// Phase 3 main loop:
//   IsCompletePrefix branch: CloseConstrainedSpan sets insideConstrainedOut := false,
//   making the implication vacuously true, and clears currentConstrainedOut := [].
//   Normal constrained branch: GroupBoostedConstrainedStep hard-masks to parser-
//   valid next tokens (plus EOS). AppendConstrainedToken extends currentConstrainedOut
//   by one parser-valid token; the parser extension property ensures
//   IsValidPrefix(currentConstrainedOut ++ [next]) holds when IsTokenValidNext holds,
//   which the hard mask guarantees. EOS+close sub-branch: CloseConstrainedSpan sets
//   insideConstrainedOut := false.
//
// Phase 4 (CloseSpanWithinBudget):
//   Helper's postcondition directly guarantees
//   insideOut ==> parser.IsValidPrefix(currentOut).
//
// Invariant 2: progress
//   |generated| <= |generatedPrefix| + steps
//
// Phase 1: Each iteration calls UnconstrainedStep (costs 1 step) and appends
//   at most 1 token to generated (0 on EOS, 1 otherwise). steps grows by 1
//   per iteration; |generated| grows by ≤1 per iteration. ✓
// Phase 2: OpenConstrainedSpan costs 1 step and appends exactly 1 "<<" token.
//   steps += 1, |generated| += 1. ✓
// Phase 3: GroupBoostedConstrainedStep costs 1 step (even for EOS). AppendConstrainedToken
